            <p>Honesty-box entry, published as a dislocation because the dislocation was ours. The Sunday walk&rsquo;s September group note quoted the Alphabet-September-crown leg (sepGOOGL) at −4.21 CHEAP against &ldquo;its 6.81 fair.&rdquo; Re-deriving the Aug 23 MC from its own published inputs: P(Alphabet largest, Sep 30) was <strong>1.39</strong>; 6.81 was P(MSFT exactly 3rd) — a transposition. At the correct fair the leg was +1.21 RICH, and this morning it reads <strong>1.95 vs 0.20 (+1.75)</strong>. No card, ticket or trade was ever built on the wrong number; the group note was wrong for one walk and is corrected here, permanently.</p>
            <div class="pm-exec"><strong>THE TICKET:</strong> <strong>None — the deliverable is the correction and the check that prevents its recurrence: every fair quoted in a group note now ties to a named row of the MC output table in the run log.</strong></div>
          </div>
          <div class="panel-card">
            <h3 class="panel-title"><span class="pm-badge pm-cheap">10 · THE RULE — VINDICATED BY TWO DEATHS</span> The edge-AND-door gate&rsquo;s record after the print: <strong>the two tickets it kept partial or unposted died at +0.98 and −2.35 with $0.00 lost</strong> · its current docket: sep3AAPL, cheap behind a $59 door</h3>
            <div class="pm-idea-date">Idea added Aug 12, 2026 <span class="pm-reviewed">· Reviewed Aug 27, 2026</span><a class="pm-card-link" href="https://polymarket.com/event/2nd-largest-company-end-of-september-20260729222928263" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open this market on Polymarket">View on Polymarket ↗</a></div>
            <p>The gate&rsquo;s ledger, updated with the week it was built for: <strong>Apple-Dec</strong> — seven walks of published edge, $150 authorised, zero filled, edge gone; <strong>the sep2AAPL fade</strong> — capped at a $223 partial by its door, never posted, edge gone. Combined realized cost of two dead flagships: <strong>zero</strong>. Against that, the rule&rsquo;s cost ledger: the Astros/gold/no-cuts exits it does NOT govern went unposted seven windows and left $139 of aggregate cheques uncashed. The gate stops bad entries; nothing on this page yet stops missed exits.</p>
            <div class="pm-exec"><strong>THE TICKET:</strong> <strong>The gate stands: ≥5 points of edge AND qualifying depth at fair, walked on the actual book, or it is a watch. New clause from #3: and no known catalyst inside the measurement window. The missing symmetrical rule for exits is the page&rsquo;s open engineering item.</strong></div>
