            <p>Invert each rung to the volatility that makes it fair at zero drift and the book stops looking irrational: <strong>4.8% → 1.94, 5.0% → 3.11, 5.2% → 3.38, 5.5% → 4.48, 5.7% → 4.97, 6.00% → 5.87 bp/day</strong>. That is a clean, monotone smile — the market pays up for tail vol and marks down near-barrier diffusion, which is what every options market on earth does. This tab has been fitting a <strong>single constant σ</strong> across all six strikes. Against a rising smile a constant σ <em>must</em> call the near rungs cheap and the far rungs rich. That is precisely the pattern this tab has reported for ten days and read as a finding. It was an assumption looking at itself.</p>
