            <div class="pm-idea-date">Idea added Aug 10, 2026 <span class="pm-reviewed">· Reviewed Aug 27, 2026</span><a class="pm-card-link" href="https://polymarket.com/event/how-high-will-10-year-treasury-yield-go-before-2027" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open this market on Polymarket">View on Polymarket ↗</a></div>
            <p>The restored pipeline lets this rung be checked against the exact series it resolves on, and the answer is sharp. The Treasury.gov daily par-yield file carries <strong>152 sessions of 2026</strong>: the highest <em>10 Yr</em> print all year is <strong>4.75% on Jul 31</strong>, today’s <strong>4.72%</strong> is the second-highest, and <strong>not one session has reached 4.80%</strong>. The barrier is <strong>8 bp</strong> above spot against a measured 10-year daily-change vol of <strong>4.3 bp</strong>, which is why the mixture says <strong>77.6</strong> against a 64.0 midpoint feed. And it is still unbuyable: no order book printed tonight, and the only executable evidence in existence is the account’s own <strong>48.06-share fill at 66.58¢ at 21:33Z</strong>, 2.6 points through the feed.</p>
            <p><strong>Friday afternoon walk (19:08Z):</strong> A book printed: <strong>63 × 167.6 / 70 × 30.2</strong>, 14 bid levels and $385 of bids, $449 of offers, mid 66.5. The 318.70-sh position (67.08¢ basis) marks $211.94, −$1.85, and <strong>walks $194.71 at a 61.10¢ VWAP over three levels</strong>. The 10Y closed 4.69% on Aug 20 — 11 bp under the barrier — and is ~4.70 intraday Friday. The ticket&rsquo;s $150 at ≤68¢ still has nothing to hit: the lowest offer is 70.</p>
            <div class="pm-exec"><strong>THE TICKET:</strong> <strong>No order. The when is a walked book with ≥300 shares inside 70¢</strong> — at that moment the ticket is $150 at ≤68¢, standalone, congruent with nothing else here. <em>Aug 12 re-check: still no book (the account added 8.96 sh at 66¢ blind, row 148 — the only print in the market); the Payoff-Book twin retired today. One run left: this row retires Aug 13 AM if no book prints.</em> <em>Aug 21 19:08Z: a book printed (63 × 168 / 70 × 30, $385 of bids); walk-out $194.71 at 61.10¢; the ≤68¢ bid would rest 2 points under the best offer — still no order.</em></div>
