            <p>The tab’s newest ticket became its fastest execution: at 01:05Z the account bought <strong>150.48 sh of the $419K–$426K bucket at a 33.89¢ average — $51.00, inside the card’s 34¢ limit and one-third under its $75 cap</strong> (ledger row 143). The book then faded beneath it: the bucket quotes <strong>28.1 × 191 / 32.6 × 27.9</strong> (mid 30.35), marking the leg <strong>−$5.18</strong> on day one — a reminder that a thin-book fill IS the market moving. The thesis is unchanged: Parcl’s feed reads $211/sqft → a $422,000 settlement, inside the bucket, and the neighbouring legs still price the index leaving it (&lt;$419K at 56.45 mid, $426–433K at 7.45). The ladder’s seven YES legs sum to ≈96.6¢ at mids — no free basket in either direction.</p>
