        <p class="pm-footnote" data-longform="3" data-longform-label="Read the sensitivity note"><strong>Sensitivity, and what actually moves these fairs.</strong> The mixture weight is the biggest lever and it is a judgement, not a measurement: at 100% martingale the 5.0% rung is <strong>49.1</strong> and at 100% AR(1) it is <strong>20.9</strong>, so the whole CHEAP/RICH verdict on the two live rungs turns on a weight this page set to 50/50 because neither model survives on its own (methodology, “The two models”). Second lever: σ. Daily-change volatility in this series has <strong>essentially no autocorrelation (0.05)</strong>, which means no trailing window forecasts forward vol — choosing 4.0 over 3.76 over 5.5 is a preference, and the 20-day estimate’s own 95% interval (2.90–5.51 bp) spans P(6%) = 2.0% to 11.9% at zero drift. Third: the barrier is monitored on the <em>daily close</em>, and the BGK shift that encodes this costs the ladder about 2 points at the near rungs — dropping it would make everything look cheaper. <strong>What this table no longer claims:</strong> that the Fed, SPX, gold, stagflation, CPI, recession and mortgage rows carry scenario information. They are marked NO MODEL. Their mids are live and their books are walked, and that is the entire contribution they make. <strong>Where the account sits:</strong> long 13,739 shares across four ladder rungs, marked $3,582.74, realisable $268.35 on tonight’s bid stacks (New #1). Books walked 22:29 UTC Aug 10, Monday post-close; mid, edge and depth columns re-baked 13:49 UTC Aug 27 (Wednesday post-print walk); every asset_id and timestamp verified in-run.</p>
