            <p>The leg&rsquo;s complete tape, for the record: listed, ran to 80.85 on the first rip, collapsed to 56.6, was bought — against this card&rsquo;s explicit no-order line — at 78.2¢ in the Friday-night sweep, bounced, and then <strong>Bitcoin printed 80,000.00 on Coinbase and $80k+ on Binance at 14:3xZ Aug 24</strong>. The account&rsquo;s six exit clips (96.4–98.8¢) hit the tape DURING the resolution spike — two ticks under par, hours before the market formally settled. Final accounting: <strong>+$82.95 realized on the violation entry; −$8.17 of par given up for immediacy</strong> (row 233, frozen). The card&rsquo;s no-order judgment was wrong on the outcome and right on the process — a 61¢ mid pricing a 3.3% squeeze was never mispriced, and the entry&rsquo;s profit was paid by the squeeze, not the price.</p>
