          <div class="panel-card">
            <h3 class="panel-title"><span class="pm-badge pm-cheap">#3 · THE LIVE WIRE AND THE DIP — THE LADDER&rsquo;S TWO CHEAP ROWS</span> <span class="pm-badge pm-watch">NEITHER HELD</span> $82.5k reach <strong>32.5 vs 38.9 (−6.4, $322 capturable)</strong> — a 4.4% squeeze with three 80-handle highs on the week&rsquo;s tape · $75k dip <strong>23.5 vs 30.4 (−6.9, $190)</strong></h3>
            <div class="pm-idea-date">Idea added Aug 21, 2026 <a class="pm-card-link" href="https://polymarket.com/event/what-price-will-bitcoin-hit-in-august-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open this market on Polymarket">View on Polymarket ↗</a></div>
            <p>Both ends of the ladder print CHEAP at the house σ, which is the model&rsquo;s way of saying the market disbelieves 2.35%/day for the last 4.6 days of August. The reach side: <strong>$82.5k at 32.5 (implied σ 2.06)</strong> — spot has printed 80,000 / 81,265 / 80,530 highs on three of the last four sessions; one more leg of the same size resolves it. The dip side: <strong>$75k at 23.5 (implied 2.03)</strong> — a −5.0% drawdown, the mirror bet. Behind them: $85k −0.8 FAIR, $87.5k +1.8, $90k <strong>+2.6 RICH</strong> (implied 2.89), $72.5k −1.4, $70k +2.0. The model holds both cheap badges honestly — and holding BOTH is a vol trade, not a direction trade.</p>
            <div class="pm-exec"><strong>THE TICKET:</strong> <strong>No order — for the account, not for the model: a fresh August touch position four sessions after liquidating the last one, with the family&rsquo;s realized −$591 still wet, fails the only test that matters this week. The $322/$190 capturable figures are published so the reader can disagree.</strong></div>
          </div>
          <div class="panel-card">
            <h3 class="panel-title"><span class="pm-badge pm-watch">#4 · THE TAIL FLOOR — THIRTEEN LEGS UNDER 2¢</span> <span class="pm-badge pm-rich">UNSELLABLE</span> Aug dips $67.5k and below plus the $100k reach: mids 0.1–1.55¢ imply σ 2.9–10.3%/day — funding floors; five legs have no bid at any price</h3>
            <div class="pm-idea-date">Idea added Aug 21, 2026 <a class="pm-card-link" href="https://polymarket.com/event/what-price-will-bitcoin-hit-in-august-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open this market on Polymarket">View on Polymarket ↗</a></div>
            <p>Mid · implied σ · bids: $100k reach <strong>0.4¢</strong> · 3.82% · $179 — $67.5k dip 1.55¢ · 3.02% · $882 — $65k 0.95¢ · 3.50% · $437 — $62.5k 0.7¢ · 4.04% · $521 — $60k 0.25¢ · 4.24% · $100 — $57.5k 0.2¢ · 4.79% · $0 — $55k 0.15¢ · 5.31% · $7 — $52.5k through $40k: 0.1–0.2¢, implied 5.8–10.3%, effectively bidless. Combined bid side across the thirteen: <strong>≈$2,126</strong>, forty percent of it on the $67.5k alone.</p>
            <p>The floor&rsquo;s function was demonstrated this week from the inside: the account&rsquo;s $90k leg — bought at 9.62¢ as a &ldquo;cheap&rdquo; tail — exited at 5.76¢ into exactly this kind of shelf. A 1–2¢ quote is a market maker&rsquo;s warehouse fee, not a probability, in both directions.</p>
