        <p class="pm-footnote" data-longform="3" data-longform-label="Read the full footnote">Four cards, one ladder, twenty-one legs (one settled), books re-walked 13:49 UTC Aug 27 against the CLOB with asset_id matched to each market&rsquo;s YES token. The week was the ladder&rsquo;s entire life cycle in miniature: a resolution (the $80k, sold into its own touch — row 233), a liquidation (rows 237–240, graded +$679 by the marks they left behind), and a survivor pair of CHEAP badges ($82.5k reach −6.4, $75k dip −6.9) that are one 2%-day from becoming the next chapter. The account&rsquo;s August exposure is ZERO for the first time since the ladder listed. Fairs are baked at σ 2.35 and T = 4.59 days; mids, edges and verdicts refresh live, and the resolved row ignores its dead token&rsquo;s residual quote.</p>
