            <p>Invert each mid to the daily σ that reproduces it under the reflection-principle model. Up: $85k <strong>1.72%</strong> · $90k <strong>1.82</strong> · $95k 1.89 · $100k <strong>1.96</strong> · $110k 2.17 · $120k 2.42 · $130k 2.45 · $140k 2.53 · $150k 2.67 · $160k 2.86. Down: $60k <strong>2.26%</strong> · $55k 2.59 · $50k 2.58 · $45k 2.99 · $40k 3.40 · $35k 3.77 · $30k 4.25 · $25k 4.48. The asymmetry is intact — and this week the up-side&rsquo;s implied σ was too LOW even ex post: an $80k touch priced at 1.8-ish vol actually printed inside three sessions.</p>
            <p>A symmetric, driftless model at 2.35% calls the up-rungs from <strong>$85k through $110k</strong> CHEAP ($95k −10.0, $90k −9.7, $100k −8.7, $85k −7.7, $110k −3.5) and the down-rungs from <strong>$55k through $30k</strong> RICH ($40k +6.5, $45k +6.2, $35k +5.3, $55k +4.4, $30k +4.3, $50k +3.1). Read literally, eleven badges; read honestly, one view — the market still expects mean reversion after the run, and pays for it on both sides.</p>
