          <div class="panel-card">
            <h3 class="panel-title"><span class="pm-badge pm-cheap">#2 · DEC $100K — THE ANCHOR, CHURNED</span> <span class="pm-badge pm-watch">6,668 SH @ 18.19¢ · +$687</span> Mid 28.5 vs fair 37.2 — the ≥25¢ distribution FILLED (5,177 sh at 25.68¢, row 242), was preceded by a 31.47¢ buy and followed by a 27.35¢ re-buy: three trades, 56 hours, a worse blend</h3>
            <div class="pm-idea-date">Idea added Aug 21, 2026 <a class="pm-card-link" href="https://polymarket.com/event/what-price-will-bitcoin-hit-before-2027" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open this market on Polymarket">View on Polymarket ↗</a></div>
            <p>Per /positions: <strong>6,668.05 sh at an 18.19¢ blend</strong>, mark <strong>$1,900.40, +$687.23</strong>, walk-out $1,744.96 over 4 levels (28 × 1,940 at the touch), 0 unfilled — an 8.2% haircut. It is 16.8% of positions on one touch and 68.8% of the BTC family. Book 28 × 1,940 / 29 × 6,573; $675.4k of asks, $29.0k of bids; DEEP. Model: $100k is 26.6% above spot, 126.6 days out; fair at σ 2.0 / 2.35 / 3.0 = <strong>29.5 / 37.2 / 48.5</strong>; the 28.5 mid implies σ 1.96 — edge <strong>−8.7</strong>, capturable <strong>$1,625 (rank #3)</strong>.</p>
            <p>The churn, scored: bought 1,573.70 at 31.47¢ the morning after the $80k touch (row 234, now −$46.74), <strong>distributed 5,176.89 at 25.68¢ twenty-eight hours later (row 242, −$146.08 against tonight&rsquo;s 28.5)</strong>, re-bought 1,491.15 at 27.35¢ (row 247, +$17.20). Net effect: 2,112 fewer shares, a blend 4.77¢ worse than the pre-week 13.42¢, and ≈−$176 of aggregate grade — the family&rsquo;s only losing week-trades were the ones on its best leg.</p>
