        <p class="pm-footnote" data-longform="3" data-longform-label="Read the sensitivity note"><strong>Sensitivity.</strong> The σ is the whole model. At σ 2.0 / 2.35 / 3.0 the Dec $100k leg is 29.4 / 37.1 / 48.4, the Dec $90k leg 55.4 / 61.4 / 69.3, the Dec $60k dip 24.2 / 31.9 / 43.5, the Aug $85k reach 21.7 / 29.3 / 41.0, the Aug $75k dip 47.2 / 54.0 / 63.1. At σ 2.0 (the 60-day realised) the $80k (−2.1) and $110k (+2.2) legs go FAIR and the $100k leg sits at −2.9, still CHEAP by four-tenths of a point, while $85k (−7.6), $90k (−5.9) and $95k (−4.8) stay CHEAP; at σ 3.0 (the 10-day realised rounded up) every RICH down-rung goes FAIR or CHEAP except $35k (+4.6) and $30k (+3.8), which stay RICH. The windows: 10d 2.97%, 20d 2.39%, 30d 2.26%, 60d 2.00%, 90d 2.12%, 349d 2.35%; Parkinson 20d 2.12%, 60d 2.04%. The house picks the longest window because the December horizon is 132 days and the shortest window is one week of catalysts — but that is a choice, and the table&rsquo;s verdicts are its consequence. What the model does not price: drift (a +25% week is not a zero-mean draw), regime change (the Aug 18–20 rule-making is a level shift in the distribution, not a sample from it), and the Binance/Coinbase basis (tens of dollars, which matters only for the Aug $80k leg). Capturable edge walks the raw ask side up to the σ 2.35 fair and sums (fair − ask) × size level by level; at σ 2.0 the $90k figure is $360, the $100k figure $25, and the Aug $75k figure zero (fair 47.2, under the 51 offer).</p>
